 into minutes:**\n   - 9 hours = 9 × 60 minutes = 540 minutes.\n\n4. **Determine the interval between each tour:** Tours are conducted every 20 minutes.\n\n5. **Calculate the number of intervals within the total time:**\n   - Number of intervals = Total time / Interval time = 540 minutes / 20 minutes = 27 intervals.\n\n6. **Determine the number of tours:** The number of tours is equal to the number of intervals plus one (since the first tour starts at 9 a.m. and counts as the first interval):\n   - Number of tours = Number of intervals + 1 = 27 + 1 = 28 tours.\n\nThus, the number of tours per day in April is \\boxed{28}."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{28}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
